            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0021",
            "textSha256": "82885c3f88cc4f8748a491740ea7b74d24d9d0199a1e7091369aa98b4f7402a2"
          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "The Beagle Channel is a striking narrow passage in the archipelago of Tierra del Fuego, a region originally named after the fires that burned in local native settlements when the first European explorers arrived. Dividing Chile and Argentina, the passage showcases ice formations along the snow-dusted Darwin Range. We will sail along Glacier Alley, home to the Holanda, Italia, Francia, Alemania, and Romanche glaciers, aiming to explore the Garibaldi Fjord."
    },
